//@version=6
indicator(title="Rain On Me ∞ V3.0d — Research & Beauty",
     shorttitle="ROM 3.0d",
     overlay=true,
     max_bars_back=1500,
     max_lines_count=200,
     max_labels_count=100,
     max_boxes_count=100)

// ╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║ V3.0d — RESEARCH & BEAUTY                                                  ║
// ║ • Preserves every V3.0a integrity and PHI-foundation contract.            ║
// ║ • Adds confirmed primary/secondary PHI geometry and cluster detection.    ║
// ║ • Gaussian resonance intensity avoids binary line-cross logic.            ║
// ║ • Adds Approach, Touch, Reject, Accept and Retest interaction states.      ║
// ║ • Adds persistent confluence beam plus bounded secondary-level visuals.   ║
// ║ • Bright rose–purple bear spectra improve readability on dark charts.    ║
// ║ • Nano-width dashboards preserve information with compact notation.      ║
// ║ • Four independent families vote: Cycle, Flow, ATR and PHI Geometry.      ║
// ║ • Dispersion, breadth and resonance produce a bounded confidence score.  ║
// ║ • Council events are bar-close gated, agreement filtered and cooled down.║
// ║ • Prospective reaction studies measure MFE, MAE and ATR response.         ║
// ║ • ROM Legacy and Canonical grids are compared on identical events.       ║
// ║ • 0.728 and 1.328 receive dedicated hidden-gem evidence tracking.         ║
// ║ • Trend/chop cohorts expose regime dependence instead of one pooled mean.║
// ║ • Evidence-weighted glow rewards tested levels without changing signals. ║
// ║ • Dynamic final alerts protect the 64-plot budget.                        ║
// ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

